  "_source": "board-en 130532 (New weapon system: Xeno Resonators FAQ, 2026-11-17): Strike +2..14% Singularity Drive damage, Aegis -2..14% Singularity damage taken by level 1-7 (C..UL); one offensive and one defensive slot per ship config; Intensify 1 main + 4 of the same type and level, success 100/100/95/85/75/65% for levels 2-7 and 1%/2% chance of a special attribute at 6/7, on failure the 4 are consumed and the main kept; Assembly: C from 10 Xeno-Tech Fragments; recycle returns fragments (client disassembly table); special attributes only on max level (client: effect operations only on the max level): Activation Chip (random), the attribute item (that attribute, replaces), Calibration Chip (+1 tier). Vortex of Greed boss drops (130529): UC 5.7%, R 10%, EP 19%, MA 15% each type; Activation Chip 0.11%, Calibration Chip 0.27%, each attribute item 0.02%. Client 1.1.119 code: window xeno_resonator (153), messages XenoResonator*, extAttributes xenoEffectId / xenoEffectLevel / xenoLocked / xenoShipId / xenoShipDamageBasisPoints, slot set xeno_resonators (belgeler/istemci/xeno_resonator_istemci.md).",
  "_adaptation": "effect weights equal (FAQ: random); SELECT keeps the tier of a replaced attribute (a new one starts at tier 1); the ship-specific drive damage bonus (xenoShipId, FAQ: \"random\") is rolled for a Strike Resonator when it is created: one of the ships with drive slots, +1..5% Singularity Drive damage on that ship, kept through Intensify; the old pre-release resonators keep their quality as level, their old attributes are dropped; Aegis only matters against enemy Singularity Drives (none in single player).",
  "_tool": "tools/version_119.py"
 },
